WEBVTT

00:00:01.500 --> 00:00:11.872
Reading Art: Art for Book Lovers is a celebration of an everyday object — the book, represented here in almost three hundred artworks from museums around the world.
《阅读艺术：献给爱书人的艺术》是对一种日常物品——书——的礼赞；这本画册收录了来自世界各地博物馆的近300件艺术作品，书的形象就呈现在这些作品之中。

00:00:12.672 --> 00:00:19.052
The image of the reader appears throughout history, in art made long before books as we now know them came into being.
读者的形象贯穿古今：早在我们今天所熟知的这种书籍问世很久以前，艺术作品中就已出现了读者的身影。

00:00:19.852 --> 00:00:26.592
In artists’ representations of books and reading, we see moments of shared humanity that go beyond culture and time.
在艺术家对书籍和阅读的描绘中，我们看到了体现人类共同天性、超越文化与时代的瞬间。

00:00:27.392 --> 00:00:35.322
In this “book of books,” artworks are selected and arranged in a way that emphasizes these connections between different eras and cultures.
在这本“书中之书”里，艺术作品的挑选和编排方式突出了不同时代、不同文化之间的这些联系。

00:00:36.122 --> 00:00:42.992
We see scenes of children learning to read at home or at school, with the book as a focus for relations between the generations.
我们看到孩子们在家中或学校里学习阅读的场景，书在其中成为代际关系的焦点。

00:00:43.792 --> 00:00:51.192
Adults are portrayed alone in many settings and poses — absorbed in a volume, deep in thought or lost in a moment of leisure.
艺术家笔下的成年人则独自一人，身处各种环境，姿态各异——或沉浸在书中，或陷入沉思，或沉醉于片刻的闲暇。

00:00:51.992 --> 00:00:57.652
These scenes may have been painted hundreds of years ago, but they record moments we can all relate to.
这些场景可能是几百年前画的，但它们记录下的是我们都能感同身受的时刻。

00:00:58.452 --> 00:01:05.282
Books themselves may be used symbolically in paintings to demonstrate the intellect, wealth or faith of the subject.
在绘画中，书本身也可能被用作象征，来展示画中人物的才智、财富或信仰。

00:01:06.082 --> 00:01:12.022
Before the wide use of the printing press, books were treasured objects and could be works of art in their own right.
在印刷机广泛使用之前，书是人们珍视的物品，其本身就可能是艺术品。

00:01:12.822 --> 00:01:25.772
More recently, as books have become inexpensive or even throwaway, artists have used them as the raw material for artworks — transforming covers, pages or even complete volumes into paintings and sculptures.
近来，随着书变得便宜，甚至成了用完就扔的东西，艺术家们便把书用作艺术创作的原材料——把封面、书页甚至整本书改造成绘画和雕塑。

00:01:26.572 --> 00:01:32.672
Continued developments in communication technologies were once believed to make the printed page outdated.
人们曾经认为，通信技术的不断发展会让印刷读物过时。

00:01:33.472 --> 00:01:41.282
From a 21st-century point of view, the printed book is certainly ancient, but it remains as interactive as any battery-powered e-reader.
从21世纪的视角来看，印刷书籍无疑是古老的，但它依然和任何一台电池驱动的电子阅读器一样具有互动性。

00:01:42.082 --> 00:01:52.824
To serve its function, a book must be activated by a user: the cover opened, the pages parted, the contents reviewed, perhaps notes written down or words underlined.
书要发挥作用，就必须由使用者来激活：掀开封面，翻开书页，浏览内容，或许还要记下笔记或在字词下画线。

00:01:53.624 --> 00:02:04.984
And in contrast to our increasingly networked lives where the information we consume is monitored and tracked, a printed book still offers the chance of a wholly private, “off-line” activity.
我们的生活日益网络化，所获取的信息受到监控和追踪；与之相比，印刷书籍仍让人有机会进行完全私密的“离线”活动。
